I have three unsubmitted manuscripts by the same authors that compute the same object. I need
a decision on whether they are three papers, two, or one. Answer as an editor would, not as a
diplomat.

THE COMMON OBJECT. Fix m. Words in {0,1}^m are assigned a Fibonacci-weighted value and folded
to the length-m golden-mean (Zeckendorf) language. The fibre multiplicities of that fold, and
their power sums S_q(m) = sum_x d_m(x)^q, are what all three papers study. I verified by
direct computation that papers A and C produce the SAME sequences up to an index shift of one:
S_q(m+1) in A equals S_q(m) in C for q = 1..4 and m = 1..12, and likewise for the maximal
fibre. The different conventions hide this - A's weights sum to F_{m+2}-1 so its fibres are
single coefficients, C's sum past F_{m+2} so its fibres are whole residue classes.

PAPER A, 47 pages. Foundation: the fibre multiplicities are Fibonacci-lag discrete derivatives
of the classical Fibonacci partition function (a "partition-difference formula"). Then:
S_q(m) squeezed between adjacent Fibonacci windows of Sanna's partition power sums, giving
S_q(m) asymptotic to lambda_q^m; each lambda_q (q>=2) identified as the Perron root of a
nonnegative integer matrix, hence an algebraic integer; the pressure sequence p_q = log
lambda_q is convex and its slopes select thickness bands with two-sided exponential estimates;
diverging tilts select the zero-temperature thickness, giving D_m^(1/m) -> sqrt(phi); and an
audited finite window q = 9..17 in which the recurrence polynomials are certified irreducible
with full symmetric Galois groups, with a product Chebotarev density for simultaneous
irreducibility on a subrange.

PAPER B, 39 pages. Carries the SAME partition-difference theorem, word for word, same label,
same notation. Then goes elsewhere: a second identity matching the complete fibre multiset to
the Fibonacci partition function on two consecutive layers; a factorization at even Zeckendorf
zero-runs determining the second-largest fibre value, all its locations and its eventual
degeneracy; an exact weighted renewal identity using the known golden-ratio Bernoulli
convolution L^q spectrum; at the freezing point an asymptotically linear critical partition
sum and a uniform coexistence law; a full large deviation principle whose rate function is
affine across the coexistence interval, obtained via an injective orbit-filling map that
supplies the nonexposed slopes; and a power-law limit for the counting measure of fibres of
multiplicity of order m.

PAPER C, 12 pages. Fixed-degree transfer: for every fixed q there is an effectively
constructible integer matrix, independent of m, whose matrix coefficient is S_q(m); the key
point is losslessness of a bounded signed-Fibonacci carry automaton. Exact recurrence
